note draft
# Checked spec, not compiled code — see ../head/mine.tree's note. The real reader is ./code.tree's
# read-otf-glyph, proven by deck/feed/test/otf-glyf.tree. Replaces the old pre-rename draft entirely (raw
# opentype.js-style JS calls — `glyphset.GlyphSet`, `glyphset.ttfGlyphLoader` — mixed into `weave`/`share`/`cause`
# syntax, not an actual byte-format description) rather than porting it. Simple glyphs only; composite glyphs
# (`number-of-contours < 0`) send `glyph-composite-unsupported`, the same shape cmap's `format-unsupported` uses.
#
# The flag run-length repeat (`read-glyf-flags`) and the two-bit-pair coordinate delta decode
# (`glyf-coordinate-delta`) are real per-byte control flow, not raw field extraction — like gzip's trailer-length
# arithmetic and loca's short-format scale, this is real-reader-only logic with no attempt at spec notation here.

mine glyph
  take byte-length, like number

  mine case, read byte-length
    case 0
      mine send, form glyph-empty
    case default
      mine int
        bind width, code 2
        bind order, term big
        bind sign, term signed
        send number-of-contours
      mine form, form short
        send x-min
      mine form, form short
        send y-min
      mine form, form short
        send x-max
      mine form, form short
        send y-max
      mine case, read number-of-contours
        case below-zero
          mine send, form glyph-composite-unsupported
        case default
          mine list
            bind count, read number-of-contours
            mine form, form ushort
            send end-points
          mine form, form ushort
            send instruction-length
          mine bytes
            bind width, read instruction-length
            send instructions
          mine flags-and-coordinates
            bind end-points, read end-points
            send contours
          mine send, form glyph-simple

mine ushort
  mine int
    bind width, code 2
    bind order, term big
    bind sign, term unsigned

mine short
  mine int
    bind width, code 2
    bind order, term big
    bind sign, term signed
